      "reasons": [
        "The packet states that Pearson’s correlation ranges from -1 for a “perfect negative relationship” to +1 for a “perfect positive relationship,” but it does not explicitly define a negative relationship as variables “moving in opposite directions.”",
        "The definition’s description of a negative relationship as “a linear association between two variables” is only indirectly supported by the packet’s statement that Pearson’s correlation measures the strength of the linear relationship; the packet does not explicitly connect this phrasing to the term “negative relationship.”",
        "Because at least one substantive element (“move in opposite directions”) is not directly supported by the provided packet text, the definition is not fully defensible."
